@TITLE@ QilinRecomp for Windows (64-bit)
=============================================

@FULL_TITLE@ (@STUDIO@), recompiled to run natively: the game's own
program translated into C++ and compiled for your PC, drawn with Vulkan.

No game data is included. You need your own copy of the game: @RELEASE@,
as a disc image.


Your disc image
---------------
An image of your disc as it is: an .iso, .gcm or .ciso file. GameCube discs
aren't encrypted, so nothing has to be extracted first. Dolphin's
compressed formats aren't read: convert an .rvz, .wia or .gcz image in
Dolphin first (right-click the game in the list, Convert File, Format: ISO).
An NKit image has to be converted back to a full one with NKit.


Playing
-------
1. Unzip the download anywhere. Building the game needs about 2 GB free.
2. Open the folder and double-click "Play @TITLE@.exe".
3. Click "Choose your disc image" and pick the file above, or drag it onto
   the window. It tells you straight away if it is the wrong game, another
   region or another revision.
4. Wait for the first build: a few minutes (up to 15 on a slower PC). Your
   game files never leave your PC.
5. Click Play. The window hides while the game runs. "Add a desktop
   shortcut" puts Play @TITLE@ on your desktop.

After that, Play @TITLE@.exe remembers your disc image (even in a new
download folder), and Play starts the game straight away. The game reads
the image while it runs, so leave it where it is (if you move it, choose it
again). After an update it builds the game again first, recompiling only
what changed.

The game's output is in work\run.log and work\run-errors.log, and the
build's in work\build.log; the game also keeps mkdd.log beside its settings
(below). Send them when reporting a problem.

If Windows says "Windows protected your PC": More info, then Run anyway.
(The download isn't signed.) Or before unpacking, right-click the zip,
Properties, tick Unblock, OK.

Needs: Windows 10 or 11, 64-bit, and a graphics driver with Vulkan 1.3
(any recent NVIDIA, AMD or Intel driver).


Controls
--------
Four GameCube controllers. Controllers take the ports in the order each
first has a button pressed; the keyboard plays the first.

  GameCube controller   Xbox controller      Keyboard (player 1)
  A                     A (bottom)           X
  B                     X (left)             Z
  X                     B (right)            C
  Y                     Y (top)              S
  Z                     RB or LB             D
  L, R                  LT, RT               A, Space
  Start                 Start                Enter
  Control stick         left stick           arrows
  C-stick               right stick          I K J L
  D-pad                 D-pad                T G F H

Back + Start together, or F1 or Esc: the settings menu (the game pauses):
controls for each player (set by pressing them), the picture (size, render
resolution, a wider picture, SMAA, FSR 1, a CRT look, frame rate), full
screen, sound. F3: frame times. F9: capture frames for a bug report.
Alt+Enter or F11: full screen.

Settings, saves, captures and the game's log are kept in
%LOCALAPPDATA%\qilin\@GAME@, with the disc image you chose and the build's
cache of compiled files (build-cache).


What's in here
--------------
Play @TITLE@.exe    chooses your disc image, builds the game (once) and starts it
kit\qilin-disc.exe  reads your disc image: takes @BOOT@ from it
kit\qilin.exe       the recompiler: turns the disc's @BOOT@ into C++, and
                    says which disc an image is
kit\qilin-dsp.exe   the same for the sound processor's program inside @BOOT@
kit\plan.tsv        which parts of the game are recompiled, and which run natively
kit\lib, include    the prebuilt rest of the game: its runtime, the disc
                    reader, the renderer, sound, the window and controls
                    (SDL3), the menu (Dear ImGui)
kit\toolchain       LLVM-MinGW, a C++ compiler for Windows (Clang)
kit\files.txt       every file this release holds (see below)
work\               made when building: the game (@EXE@), built from your
                    disc, the recompiled code, the build's files and the logs
LICENSES\           the licences of everything included

Source, changes and issues: https://github.com/Qilin1066/MarioKartDD--QilinRecomp


Updates and recovery
--------------------
"Check for updates" in Play @TITLE@.exe asks GitHub for a newer release of
@FULL_TITLE@ (it sends nothing about you or your PC). If there is one, it
downloads it, unpacks it beside this folder and swaps in the new kit and
launcher, then starts again and builds the game for the new version. If
anything fails on the way, the old version is left as it was. You can also
unzip a new download anywhere, even over this folder: it finds your disc
image and the cache by itself, and at its first start it removes what an
older version left behind (the Play @TITLE@.bat, play.ps1 and Ninja of the
first downloads, and files the new kit no longer has: anything in kit\ or
LICENSES\ that kit\files.txt doesn't name). Your saves and settings are
never in this folder, so nothing of yours is touched.

The game is compiled for this PC's processor; moved to another PC, it is
built again. Compiled files come from the cache when nothing they're made
from has changed. A failed build leaves the working game as it was; the one
before a new build is kept as work\@EXE@.previous until the new one has run
and closed normally. "Build again from scratch" compiles everything anew.

Before the game writes to a memory card, the save it replaces is kept: the
five most recent of each. The settings menu's Game page, Previous saves,
restores one and restarts (backing up the current save first).
